\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Features $C$ and $D$ for the 114 cleaned training samples (filled) and the 30 test samples (hollow, drawn in their predicted class), with the $2\sigma $ density contour of each fitted class Gaussian and its centroid marked by a cross. Class 1 is well separated; classes 2 and 3 overlap, and that overlap is where the closest test decisions (17, 23, 30) and the five training errors lie. Row 91's outlier ($C = 16.0$) and row 117's ($D = 5.3$) fall outside the plotted range, and row 96's outlier is in feature $A$.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cd}{{1}{5}{Features $C$ and $D$ for the 114 cleaned training samples (filled) and the 30 test samples (hollow, drawn in their predicted class), with the $2\sigma $ density contour of each fitted class Gaussian and its centroid marked by a cross. Class 1 is well separated; classes 2 and 3 overlap, and that overlap is where the closest test decisions (17, 23, 30) and the five training errors lie. Row 91's outlier ($C = 16.0$) and row 117's ($D = 5.3$) fall outside the plotted range, and row 96's outlier is in feature $A$}{figure.1}{}}
